# Headless browser scratch.
# `npm run parity` drives a real Chrome to get a WebGL context and needs a
# user-data dir for it. It currently lands under node_modules, which is already
# ignored, but pin the names too so a relocated profile cannot get committed.
.parity-chrome
chrome-profile*

